{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "30c30a89-6201-8189-b35d-359f6935dc84",
  "created_at": "2026-01-14T14:04:07-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Daniela Rivera",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:00:17-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:00:20-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, good afternoon. I'm calling about a recycling bin that didn't get picked up. It has a tag on it saying it was rejected."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:00:30-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, sure. Where's the bin located?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:00:33-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 239 Marsh Street, in the Point. I manage the property, I don't live there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:00:39-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 239 Marsh. And when was the pickup that got skipped?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:00:44-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "This week. Monday, I think, was the day on that street. And this is the second miss in a row. Last time it was the same thing, the bin just sat there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:00:57-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright, second time in a row. Did the first one have a tag too, or just left alone?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:01:04-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Last time no tag, I just saw it still full on the curb. This time there is a tag. It's orange, kind of a sticker on the lid, and it says rejected."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:01:16-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Does it say a reason on there? Usually they check a box, like contamination, or bagged items, something like that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:01:25-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me look, I'm not at the house right now, I'm in the car. [pause] Sorry, one second. Mamãe, no, nu ta bai ali agora, nu ta fala ku el. Okay, sorry. My aunt is with me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:01:39-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:01:42-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I have a picture on my phone. It says, um, non-recyclable materials. That's the box that's checked."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:01:49-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's the contamination one. So something in the bin wasn't accepted. Usually that's things like plastic bags, food containers with food still in them, or garden waste mixed in."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:02:01-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I think I know what it is. The tenants might put trash bags inside. I do work for a landscaping crew, but they're off for the winter, so I've been handling the buildings more myself, and I'm not there every day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:02:17-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Gotcha, so you're picking up the slack while the crew's on break. That makes sense. So what do you need from us, just the bin picked up, or information on what's allowed?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:02:29-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both, really. Can somebody come back for it? And is there a list of what they accept so I can put it up for the tenants?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:02:39-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me note this down. Two-three-nine Marsh Street, recycling bin rejected for non-recyclables, second miss in a row, caller is the property manager. Right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:02:49-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:02:51-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Typically, once a bin gets rejected, you need to take out the stuff that doesn't belong and put it out again on your next regular recycling day. They don't usually come back in between. But I'll put in a note so the supervisor sees that it's twice."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:03:09-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So I take the bags out and wait until the next collection."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:03:15-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. And bagged recyclables are the big one. Everything goes in loose. Rinse out containers, flatten cardboard. We have a flyer with the full list, and it's on the city website under the trash and recycling page. I can also mail one out if you give me a mailing address."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:03:34-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Mail it to the same address, 239 Marsh Street. Then I can post it in the hallway."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:03:41-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Will do. I'll send a couple of copies. Is the best number to reach you the one you're calling from?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:03:49-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, it's 401-555-0162."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:03:51-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect, 401-555-0162. If the supervisor has anything to add, somebody will call you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:03:57-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, thank you. That's all I needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:04:01-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got it, Daniela. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T14:04:05-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
